From: Mateusz Krawczuk <mateusz.krawczuk@cybrixsystems.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: tegra194: enable EQOS multi-queue operation

The Tegra194 EQOS node carries no snps,mtl-rx-config / snps,mtl-tx-config
subnodes.  stmmac_mtl_setup() therefore falls back to its hardcoded
default of a single RX and a single TX queue:

	plat->rx_queues_to_use = 1;
	plat->tx_queues_to_use = 1;

so the whole gigabit RX path is served by one DMA channel driven by one
NAPI context.  With the single shared MAC interrupt this pins all RX
softirq processing to a single CPU; on a Xavier devkit /proc/interrupts
shows every one of the ~415k end0 interrupts landing on CPU0 while the
remaining seven cores stay idle.

The hardware is not so limited.  MAC_HW_Feature2 reports four RX and
four TX DMA channels and four RX/TX MTL queues (dwmac4_get_hw_feature()
adds one to the raw RXCHCNT/TXCHCNT fields, so the value surfaced in
debugfs is already the total, despite the "Additional" label):

	Number of Additional RX channel: 4
	Number of Additional TX channel: 4
	Number of Additional RX queues: 4
	Number of Additional TX queues: 4

Describe all four queues in DT.  Strict-priority scheduling and the
identity queue-to-channel mapping match the defaults used by other
dwc-qos-ethernet-4.10 users.  The 64 KiB RX and TX FIFOs are split
evenly by the driver, leaving 16 KiB per queue, which is still well
above the 8 KiB threshold at which dwmac4 enables store-and-forward.

Per-channel interrupts are deliberately not added: stmmac_dma_interrupt()
iterates channels_to_check and services every DMA channel from the single
MAC interrupt, so multi-queue does not depend on the multi-MSI path.
Splitting the interrupt would be a separate change.

Note that enabling multi-queue on stmmac has regressed other platforms
before -- sa8155p ended up reverting to a single queue after RX stalls --
so this must be validated under sustained load together with the RX
refill fix carried as patch 0011.

Upstream-Status: Pending (candidate for upstream; queue count taken from
the IP's own MAC_HW_Feature2 register on T194)
Signed-off-by: Mateusz Krawczuk <mateusz.krawczuk@cybrixsystems.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194.dtsi
@@ -164,6 +164,62 @@
 			snps,burst-map = <0x7>;
 			snps,txpbl = <16>;
 			snps,rxpbl = <8>;
+			snps,mtl-rx-config = <&eqos_mtl_rx_setup>;
+			snps,mtl-tx-config = <&eqos_mtl_tx_setup>;
+
+			eqos_mtl_rx_setup: rx-queues-config {
+				snps,rx-queues-to-use = <4>;
+				snps,rx-sched-sp;
+
+				queue0 {
+					snps,dcb-algorithm;
+					snps,priority = <0x1>;
+					snps,map-to-dma-channel = <0>;
+				};
+
+				queue1 {
+					snps,dcb-algorithm;
+					snps,priority = <0x2>;
+					snps,map-to-dma-channel = <1>;
+				};
+
+				queue2 {
+					snps,dcb-algorithm;
+					snps,priority = <0x4>;
+					snps,map-to-dma-channel = <2>;
+				};
+
+				queue3 {
+					snps,dcb-algorithm;
+					snps,priority = <0x8>;
+					snps,map-to-dma-channel = <3>;
+				};
+			};
+
+			eqos_mtl_tx_setup: tx-queues-config {
+				snps,tx-queues-to-use = <4>;
+				snps,tx-sched-sp;
+
+				queue0 {
+					snps,dcb-algorithm;
+					snps,priority = <0x1>;
+				};
+
+				queue1 {
+					snps,dcb-algorithm;
+					snps,priority = <0x2>;
+				};
+
+				queue2 {
+					snps,dcb-algorithm;
+					snps,priority = <0x4>;
+				};
+
+				queue3 {
+					snps,dcb-algorithm;
+					snps,priority = <0x8>;
+				};
+			};
 		};
 
 		gpcdma: dma-controller@2600000 {
